                        "cwe": "CWE-704",
                        "severity": "Medium",
                        "reasoning": "The `Proxy.newProxyInstance` call creates a proxy that only implements the `ConnectionProxy` interface, but it is cast to and returned as a `java.sql.Connection`. Since the proxy does not implement the `java.sql.Connection` interface, any attempt by the application to use the returned object as a `Connection` (e.g., calling `prepareStatement` or `createStatement`) will result in a `ClassCastException` at runtime. While this is a functional bug, it creates a potential Denial of Service (DoS) condition for any database-dependent feature in the application that relies on this `DataSource`.",
                        "mitigation": "Include `java.sql.Connection.class` in the array of interfaces passed to `Proxy.newProxyInstance` so that the proxy correctly implements the expected interface.",
